# Google OAuth Client ID used by the "Google Docs" export button.
# This is a PUBLIC client ID, not a secret — it is safe to expose in
# frontend code. No client secret is used anywhere in this app.
#
# Setup (Google Cloud Console):
#   1. console.cloud.google.com -> select/create a project
#   2. APIs & Services -> Library -> enable "Google Drive API"
#   3. APIs & Services -> OAuth consent screen -> configure it
#      (scope needed: https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.file)
#   4. APIs & Services -> Credentials -> Create Credentials
#      -> OAuth client ID -> Application type: "Web application"
#   5. Under "Authorized JavaScript origins" add this app's dev and
#      production URLs (e.g. http://localhost:5173 and your deployed
#      domain). No redirect URI is needed for this flow.
#   6. Copy the generated Client ID below.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
